Forager patch 0008: each line, name, shield, place, POI and label goes into the tiles at openstreetmap-carto v6.1.0's
first zoom N minus 2, and polygons are kept from a quarter pixel (dispatch 2026-11-02-coder-13; the owner: "set it to
OSM zoom levels", "on the entire map").

Against protomaps/basemaps at ca93fc06efbaff1c5f069d06edbe5de18839c1c8 (tiles 4.15.2), with 0001 to 0007 already
applied. Applied after them with `git apply` by map-build/bin/build-basemap-jar.sh.

Why N - 2: the app's OpenStreetMap map is a 256 px raster, and MapLibre shows carto's tile level N from camera N - 1.5;
our 512 px vector tiles draw level z from camera z (Juniper's comparison, Forager osm-zoom-levels 53c5d6801, A1b; the
planner's decision of 14:36). The style's minzoom goes to N - 1.5 (Forager osm-zooms-style), so a feature has to be
in our tiles from level N - 2. Every value is carto's rule at v6.1.0, cited in the code by file and line.

- Roads: lines (FORAGER_OSM_LINE_ZOOMS: motorway and trunk 4, primary 6, secondary 7, tertiary and links 8,
  residential and unclassified 10, road 8, raceway 10, living street 11, service 12 and driveways 14, pedestrian,
  path, footway and steps 12, track, cycleway and bridleway 11), names (trunk to secondary 11, tertiary 12, streets,
  living streets, pedestrian streets and tracks 13) and shields (motorway 8, trunk and primary 9, secondary 10,
  tertiary 11). The class decides, as on carto: no US route-network zoom, and access=private or no keeps the class's
  zoom, except paths and tracks carto's int_access calls "no" (13). Bridges with their own casing from 11 (motorway to
  secondary; others 12), tunnels from 10 (motorway to tertiary) and 11 (streets). Links are kept from 8 (LinkSimplify
  only below 8). Rail from 6 (preserved 10, tram and subway 10, spurs, sidings and yards 11, disused 13), piers from 10
  with no size floor below 13, taxiways from 9.
- Water: rivers 6, streams 10, intermittent and seasonal streams 11; water polygons from a quarter pixel (upstream 1);
  lake labels at carto's first level over 3000 px (5 to 16) minus 2, from 3, else 15.
- Landuse: polygons from a quarter pixel, by setMinPixelSize and by the bounding-box filter below 15 (upstream 2 px and
  1.5625 px2, more at 6 and below).
- Boundaries: admin_level 5 from 6 (upstream 8), 7 from 9 (upstream 10).
- Places: carto's rules (city score of population or 100,000, doubled for capital=4: 2 at 3,000,000, 3 at 400,000,
  4 at 70,000, else 5; national capitals 2 over 600,000, else 3; town 7, village 10, hamlet 12, isolated dwelling and
  farm 13, locality 14, suburb 10, quarter 12, neighbourhood 13), over places.csv's zooms.
- POIs: peaks 9, alpine and wilderness huts 11, camp sites, picnic sites, viewpoints and shelters 14, parking 12 over
  750 px at 14 else 15; area names by carto's tag groups (forest, wood, national park, protected area, nature reserve
  from 8; leisure=park from 10) at the first level over 3000 px minus 2, else 15.
- Islands: the label at carto's first level over 3000 px (from 4) minus 2, else 14, with no 20 px floor.

Unchanged: Natural Earth at low zooms, the min_zoom attributes and sort keys of roads (label priority), POI thinning,
kinds the tiles don't write (saddles, heath, wetland subtypes, ditch and canal styles; Juniper's B2).

Tests: 72 upstream and earlier-Forager cases updated to these zooms, each marked "Forager patch 0008", and 77 new
foragerOsm* cases (RoadsTest 35, PlacesTest 16, PoisTest 9, WaterTest 6, BoundariesTest 5, LanduseTest 4,
EarthTest 2). 590 tests, 0 failures.

